As I described above, knowledge about the game is very important in
nethack.  However, patience is very useful; I know that sometimes when
I'm playing too fast (trying to ascend from scratch before I go to bed
or some such crazy idea) I have a tendency to find one way out of
situations that has some chance of success and use it right away; I
used to do this even in normal games.  It makes a big difference to,
after realizing you're in a tough situation, sit down and think
everything through, consult spoilers where necessary, and make sure you
know what all the options are before you pick one.  It's not as
important as the knowledge required to do the rest of what I just
described, but it's still a necessary factor for success, in my
opinion.

